@startuml MCP Integration Workflow

!theme plain
title SABER MCP Integration - Command Execution Workflow

actor Agent
participant "ServerClient" as Client
participant "SessionRestAPI\n(REST)" as REST
participant "SessionMCPAPI\n(MCP Component)" as MCP
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "ExecutionManager" as EM
participant "TaskManager" as TM

== Session Initialization ==
Agent -> Client: initialize()
Client -> REST: POST /session
REST -> SM: create_session()
SM -> Client: session_id
Client -> MCP: connect_mcp(session_id)
MCP -> SM: map_session_context()
MCP -> Client: mcp_connected

== Episode Start ==
Agent -> Client: start_episode(task_id)
Client -> REST: POST /session/{id}/start-episode
REST -> SM: start_episode()
SM -> TM: start_episode()
TM -> SM: episode_info
SM -> Client: episode_started

== Tool Discovery ==
Agent -> Client: get_available_tools()
Client -> MCP: list_tools()
MCP -> SM: get_execution_manager()
SM -> EM: to_mcp_tools()
EM -> MCP: tool_schemas[]
MCP -> Client: mcp_tools[]
Client -> Agent: available_tools[]

== Command Execution ==
Agent -> Client: execute_command(tool_name, args)
Client -> MCP: call_tool(tool_name, args)
MCP -> SM: execute_command(session_id, action)
SM -> EM: step(action, context)
EM -> SM: command_result
SM -> TM: step(session_id, action, result)
TM -> SM: step_result
SM -> MCP: execution_result
MCP -> Client: mcp_result
Client -> Agent: command_result

== Session Cleanup ==
Agent -> Client: close_session()
Client -> MCP: disconnect()
MCP -> SM: cleanup_mcp_session()
Client -> REST: DELETE /session/{id}
REST -> SM: terminate_session()
SM -> Client: session_closed

note right of MCP
**SessionMCPAPI Responsibilities**
- Tool discovery from ExecutionManager
- Command execution delegation only
- Session context mapping
- Protocol translation (MCP ↔ SessionManager)
- NO policy, session, or episode management
end note

note right of REST
**SessionRestAPI Responsibilities**
- Session lifecycle management
- Episode management
- Policy access
- Status monitoring
- Event streaming
- Health checks
end note

note right of SM
**SessionManager Coordination**
- Unified backend for both protocols
- Contains and manages MCP component
- Session state management
- Component orchestration
- Security and validation
end note

@enduml
